---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="ESNNA Prevention | PDT Peruvian Travel" 
    description="Firm commitment against the Sexual Exploitation of Children and Adolescents (ESNNA) in the tourism sector."
>
    <Breadcrumb 
        title="ESNNA Code of Conduct" 
        image="/bc-gallery.avif" 
        alt="ESNNA" 
        lang="en" 
    />
    
    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 bg-white">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Our Commitment</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed text-justify">
            At <strong>PDT Peruvian Travel</strong>, we are deeply committed to preventing and condemning the Sexual Exploitation of Children and Adolescents (ESNNA) in the context of travel and tourism. We recognize that tourism must be an engine for sustainable development and the protection of human rights.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed text-justify">
            As a responsible travel agency registered under the guidelines of the Ministry of Foreign Trade and Tourism (MINCETUR), we strictly adhere to current Peruvian legislation (Law N° 28251) and other regulations that seek to eradicate and penalize any practice that violates the physical or psychological integrity of minors.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Our Agency Policies:</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-8">
            <li><strong>Zero tolerance:</strong> We do not allow or facilitate any sort of activity, either direct or indirect, that involves the exploitation of minors.</li>
            <li><strong>Continuous training:</strong> We keep our entire staff alert and equipped to recognize situations of risk and properly interact to prevent them.</li>
            <li><strong>Constant collaboration:</strong> We work together with hotels, restaurants, local operators, and government authorities to ensure clean, ethical, and safe tourism.</li>
            <li><strong>Mandatory reporting:</strong> We have the obligation and moral duty to report any suspicion of ESNNA related networks to the Peruvian National Police and competent authorities.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Help Us Protect the Children</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed text-justify">
            We invite all our travelers, collaborators, and clients to play an active role in this cause. Sustainable tourism respects the host community and protects its most vulnerable. If you witness or suspect a case of exploitation, please do not hesitate to report it confidentially to the National Police, or by calling the toll-free number <strong>1818</strong> (Peru).
        </p>
    </main>
</Layout>
